@yiyunet/dsh-kill-ai-slop README · ① Browser GUI (`dsh web` / `dsh --profile web`)：```sh
dsh plugin --profile web add @yiyunet/dsh-kill-ai-slop
```

@yiyunet/dsh-kill-ai-slop README · Two words: AI Slop and Work Slop：What they share: **neither asks "who wrote it" — both ask "how much effort does this file push onto you."**
That is why this plugin guesses no author and reports no "AI probability".

> Why execution and decision carry 80%: a terse but fact-rich report is merely *not pretty*;
> a proposal with no purpose, no support and no owner gets sent back for rework —
> **that is the real cost.**

---

@yiyunet/dsh-kill-ai-slop README · Why not a single "AI rate"：**The three are weighted into a single 体检得分 (0–100, higher = worse).** Execution and decision carry 80% because this plugin targets *work slop*, not prose style — a terse but fact-rich technical report must not be judged bad for "not reading like prose".

> Weights `20 / 40 / 40` are **provisional and uncalibrated**. A steering wheel, not a ruler for performance reviews.

---

@yiyunet/dsh-kill-ai-slop README · Use it：Settings → **ANB 工具** → **AI垃圾过滤** (`anb.tool.tab`, `order: 20`):

1. Drop a file, or paste text;
2. pick a **document type** (this is an applicability switch, not a style option);
3. press **开始体检** (run audit);
4. read four tabs — overview / evidence / distillation / raw Markdown.

Nothing leaves the machine: the browser hands the bytes to the local DSH host process, which scores them in memory.

@yiyunet/dsh-kill-ai-slop README · Supported files：- a `.docx` that actually contains a spreadsheet / web page / plain text / PDF → **parsed by its real
  format**, with an explicit "extension does not match content" note in the report;
- a `.docx` that is really a legacy `.doc`, or a password-protected Office file → each gets **one**
  concrete next action (re-save / remove the password);
- starts like a ZIP but has no central directory, or is too short to be a complete container → treated
  as a truncated download, not vaguely reported as "not a ZIP".

@yiyunet/dsh-kill-ai-slop README · Fidelity-first extraction：Numbers, dates, owners, commitments and conditional outcomes are **hard-protected**: they are force-included at every compression level. Retention is guaranteed structurally, not checked after the fact.

Three levels: integrity (structure kept) / summary (default, reorganised by element) / card (≤3 lines per element, explicitly "not a substitute for the original"). Every level reports what was dropped and why.

---

